{
  "slug": "nawy-launches",
  "projectSlug": "nawy",
  "title": "Website",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "k5zmowr6",
      "title": "The problem\n",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "71wny0i8",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "vc59xdqk",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Nawy is the largest proptech platform in Africa. Listings and search are where most people decide whether to keep exploring or leave, and 58% of them left."
              },
              {
                "id": "v8ozbt8k",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Listings were structured compound-first: you browsed compounds, then drilled in to find units. That mirrored how sales qualified a lead on the phone, \"Which compound are you interested in?\", and stakeholders were confident it was right."
              },
              {
                "id": "un1d7uvn",
                "kind": "pullquote",
                "text": "A 73% drop-off on the most important page in the product is not a styling problem."
              },
              {
                "id": "bnw0t4zx",
                "kind": "image",
                "src": "/uploads/1784396541239-Screenshot-2026-07-18-at-5.38.15-PM.webp",
                "alt": "",
                "caption": "",
                "ratio": "wide",
                "fit": "natural"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "eqtdt4yt",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            []
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "yr55iimi",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            []
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "problem"
    },
    {
      "id": "swyj9p8w",
      "title": "What research showed\n",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "lfvh30ha",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "xnoithxa",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "I ran interviews with buyers to map how they actually search for a home. The finding was consistent, and it contradicted the model the product was built on."
              },
              {
                "id": "c1nhrw0y",
                "kind": "quote",
                "text": "I want a 3-bedroom apartment in a compound like SODIC.",
                "attribution": "The pattern across interviews"
              },
              {
                "id": "5wxd12a3",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Buyers search unit-first. The compound is an attribute of the unit, a filter on it, not the way in. The old structure forced people to do the platform's filtering for it: pick a compound, then hope the right unit existed inside. If it didn't, they bounced."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "research"
    },
    {
      "id": "liz6a9wo",
      "title": "The structure was the problem",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "mfa541za",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "vsycrse9",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "The mismatch wasn't visual. It was structural. The product's information architecture asked a question buyers weren't ready to answer."
              },
              {
                "id": "80p4atqt",
                "kind": "pullquote",
                "text": "The product was organised around how the company sold. Buyers were organised around how they live."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "structure"
    },
    {
      "id": "gsmdc4pp",
      "title": "The decision I had to argue for",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "0n1317fb",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "5cinnqu5",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "Keep compound-first"
              },
              {
                "id": "kq33rufp",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "It matches the sales script, needs no data restructuring, and nobody has to be convinced. But it keeps asking buyers to name a compound before they can see a single unit."
              },
              {
                "id": "olvjv1qd",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "Lead with the unit"
              },
              {
                "id": "yanfa4k3",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "The card surfaces the unit, its type, size and key details, with the compound name beside it as context. Tapping a compound then reveals the units inside it."
              },
              {
                "id": "at7j0h3w",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "A restructure of how results were assembled, and a harder conversation with stakeholders. I brought the interviews and the drop-off number rather than an opinion, and kept the compound view one tap away behind a property/compound switch, so the change read as an addition, not a rejection of how sales worked."
              },
              {
                "id": "452kw1hc",
                "kind": "beforeAfter",
                "before": "/uploads/1784396792783-Area-Search-Properties.webp",
                "after": "/uploads/1784396939946-Area-Search-Compound.webp",
                "caption": "Drag to compare."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ri81cqh1",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            []
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "3onrhr6r",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            []
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "decision"
    },
    {
      "id": "p6c7rf0e",
      "title": "Filters people could actually use",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "qyrui1aq",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "pff9u9ds",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "The filter set had grown by accretion. Every request added another control, and the ones that decided a purchase were buried among the ones that didn't. I reordered them around the decisions buyers actually make."
              },
              {
                "id": "9jpm495b",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "Payment plans and instalment years promoted to first-class filters",
                  "not footnotes",
                  "Property type and finishing expanded",
                  "because buyers genuinely filter on both",
                  "Every filter group resets independently",
                  "so nobody has to start over to change one thing"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "hrmiaqk1",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "The test wasn't whether the filters looked cleaner. It was whether someone could go from \"I have EGP 20K a month\" to a shortlist without asking anyone."
              },
              {
                "id": "bfei9j9w",
                "kind": "image",
                "src": "/uploads/1784397421044-Filters.webp",
                "alt": "",
                "caption": "",
                "ratio": "wide",
                "fit": "natural"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "4a1zx62o",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            []
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "filter"
    },
    {
      "id": "hut3yd2i",
      "title": "Removing the sticker shock",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "lt31twey",
          "layout": "2-1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "w7d9o6ch",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "A second research thread looked at how developers actually price and sell. Leading with the full property price created sticker shock. People bounced on a number in the millions before they understood that nobody pays it at once."
              },
              {
                "id": "rpfqq1ug",
                "kind": "table",
                "head": [
                  "Before",
                  "After"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "Starts at EGP 9M",
                    "Down payment from EGP 150K · instalments up to 9 years"
                  ],
                  [
                    "",
                    "or from EGP 20K / month"
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "b4v396w2",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Tapping the card now goes straight into the payment plan, so people explore affordability instead of bouncing on a big number. It widened reach to affordability-driven buyers, who were then qualified in the CRM, so volume didn't come at the cost of lead quality."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "id": "84lwtsuq",
                "kind": "image",
                "src": "/uploads/1784575868896-iPhone-16-Pro-mockup-natural-titanium.webp",
                "alt": "",
                "caption": "",
                "ratio": "wide",
                "fit": "natural",
                "framed": false,
                "size": "column"
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "speed"
    },
    {
      "id": "fr0ud6qo",
      "title": "Also shipped",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "o8pz04yk",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "ol726bbb",
